From 748f0236b15c706bc4cf6d5eacc3cbc8d8f1bfc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 07:12:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] metal: lift TQ3_4S kernel set from tq3/master (5 files +
 alloc hook)

Ports the TQ3_4S Metal support from the tq3 fork tip (source commit
02d51f048, metal: add TQ3_4S GPU support #59): E3M5 scale decode +
3-bit unpack helpers and local dequantize_tq3_4s, the forward-RHT
activation pre-pass kernel (kernel_tq3_4s_rht_f32), the coalesced
mat-vec (kernel_mul_mv_tq3_4s_f32), the one-SIMD-group-per-row
get_rows kernel, and the mul_mm GEMM template instance. Host side:
pipeline getters, N_R0/N_SG tuning constants, kargs_tq3_rht, the
dedicated ggml_metal_op_mul_mat_tq3_4s path, and the extra_w1
scratch sizing in the Metal alloc-size hook.

FIX KEPT ON PURPOSE: tq3/master TIP has the dispatch hook displaced
into ggml_metal_op_mul_mat_id by the b745799e7 rebase, which strands
the MUL_MAT-only scratch (extra_w1) and would run mul_mat_id with an
unallocated buffer. This port restores the hook to
ggml_metal_op_mul_mat, where the source commit 02d51f048 put it.

NOT BUILT HERE: this rig has no Apple silicon or Metal toolchain.
Compile readiness only; hardware validation is an OWED row with
verbatim commands in the lane evidence (HARDWARE-VALIDATION.md).

Taken-from: turbo-tan/llama.cpp-tq3@854516439
Origin: lane-160 TQ3_4S hunk port; dispatch-hook placement restored to the 02d51f048 original (tip regression); TQ3_4S-only trim
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED ON THIS RIG (no Metal silicon); tq3-side reference: M3 Pro 27B decode ~4 t/s, ~27x over CPU (02d51f048)
Lane: lane-160
